# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MSUI Client
#
# The first rule is the important one. GameData holds the WoW 1.12.1
# client archives and a copy of the server's extracted vmaps: several
# gigabytes of Blizzard's files that must never enter this history. Once
# a large blob is committed it stays in the pack forever unless the
# history is rewritten, and GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB
# on push - so the failure arrives late, after the commit, when it is
# most annoying to undo.
#
# Verify before the first commit:
#     git check-ignore -v GameData
# It should print this file and the line number. Silence means it is NOT
# ignored, and you should stop and fix that before staging anything.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GameData/
*.MPQ
*.mpq
*.vmo
*.vmtile
*.adt
*.wdt
*.dbc

# Extracted client UI art. `Interface/` at the repo root is a loose dump of
# interface.MPQ's Interface\ tree - 52 MB of Blizzard's files, the same class
# of content as GameData and ignored for the same reason. Nothing needs the
# loose copy: WowSkin reads the .blp files straight out of the archive at
# runtime, and tools/mpqpeek reads them offline.
Interface/

# Reference source copied in from another project for reading, not for
# building. WoWee is someone else's code and must not enter this history;
# the handbook's lineage section is where its findings get recorded.
_wowee_ref/

# vmangos server-emulator source, vendored as a read-only spell-behavior
# reference. It carries its own .git (24 MB); it must not be embedded as a
# gitlink or copied into this history. Recoverable independently via its own repo.
.reference-vmangos-core/

# Per-machine paths. client-config.json.example is committed instead, so
# a fresh clone has a template without carrying anyone's local layout.
client-config.json
local-credentials/

# Per-user preferences written by the settings modal (Escape). Taste, not
# wiring: it holds view distance, clutter density, water look and any named
# presets. Ignored for the same reason client-config.json is - it is one
# person's machine. The built-in quality levels live in code (GameSettings
# .ApplyQuality), so a fresh clone is never short of a sane starting point.
settings.json

# Archives produced by setup-vmaps.ps1
*.tar.gz
vmaps.tar.gz

# ── .NET build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.cache
project.lock.json
project.assets.json
*.nuget.props
*.nuget.targets

# ── Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code ──────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.userprefs

# Per-user assistant/editor state. Project-wide agent instructions belong in
# AGENTS.md or .agents/, not in these local settings.
/.claude/

# ImGui writes window positions and sizes here at runtime.
/imgui.ini

# ── OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── Documentation policy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root-level .md docs are tracked (owner decision 2026-08-11: feature handbooks
# like NPC_DEV_WINDOW.md / CRPG_RTS_WIP.md live at the root and must be pushable).
# Keep the root to REAL maintained docs - scratch notes go in /can delete or move/.

/docs/*
!/docs/README.md
!/docs/current/
!/docs/current/**
!/docs/systems/
!/docs/systems/**
!/docs/plans/
!/docs/plans/**

# Explicitly local/disposable holding area.
/can delete or move/

# ── Scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
scratch/
# Scene dumps (dev tool output; regenerated on demand)
dumps/
# Regenerable pixel evidence from --portrait-batch (often >1 GiB per full run)
portrait-batch/*
!portrait-batch/baseline/
!portrait-batch/baseline/verdicts.csv
# Regenerable character-variant evidence. Keep only the canonical machine
# baseline; contact sheets and per-specimen PNGs remain local review artifacts.
variant-batch/*
!variant-batch/baseline/
variant-batch/baseline/*
!variant-batch/baseline/npc-extras/
variant-batch/baseline/npc-extras/*
!variant-batch/baseline/npc-extras/verdicts.csv
!variant-batch/baseline/npc-extras/*.keys
!variant-batch/baseline/items/
variant-batch/baseline/items/*
!variant-batch/baseline/items/verdicts.csv
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# NIGHT_02 parity-harness development captures superseded by the immutable
# 20260801-153500 proof packet. Retained locally; not acceptance evidence.
live-runs/N2-0-1-parity-harness-20260801-151500/
live-runs/N2-0-1-parity-harness-20260801-151900/
live-runs/N2-0-1-parity-harness-20260801-152400/
live-runs/N2-0-1-parity-harness-20260801-153000/
live-runs/N2-0-1-parity-harness-20260801-160000/
live-runs/N2-0-2-1-unit-frames-20260801-154500/
live-runs/N2-0-2-1-unit-frames-20260801-155000/

# --- session evidence (untracked, kept on disk) ---
/live-runs/
/dumps/
/scenarios/
/movement-scenarios/
/movement-scripts/
/combat-instruments/
/scratch/
/portrait-batch/
/variant-batch/
/NIGHT_01/
/NIGHT_02/
/NIGHT_03/
/NIGHT_04/
/NIGHT_05/
/NIGHT_06/
/NIGHT_07/
/NIGHT_*/
/_to_delete/

# Benilla/MSUI clinical parity workspace. Snapshots, generated reports, packet
# workspaces, copied source evidence, screenshots, and historical ledger
# iterations are local/regenerable artifacts and must not enter Git. The
# durable reviewed state is the current trace + claim ledger below.
/parity/snapshots/
/parity/reports/
/parity/packets/
/parity/claims/*
!/parity/claims/current.jsonl
/parity/traces/*
!/parity/traces/current.jsonl
/parity/config.local.json

# Parity working data that stays out of history: archive/ is the retired
# packet-machinery corpus (34k files, 1.2 GB), verification/ the raw triage
# evidence batches (96 MB). The registry/ tree is the source of truth and IS
# committed; these two are its bulk inputs, reproducible and unreviewable.
parity/archive/
parity/verification/

# NPC dev window: cached DB exports (regenerated on demand from MangosSuperUI)
/dev-cache/
